  "description": "As with Star Wars, The Empire Strikes Back awed viewers with a parade of bizarre alien life forms and other far-out, highly imaginative creations. The majority of the concept art and designs for the film were rendered by Ralph McQuarrie, Joe Johnston and Nilo Rodis-Jamero, based on ideas by Lucas. Yoda became the new superstar of Empire, brought to convincing life in puppet form by British make-up artist Stuart Freeborn. He claims he based Yoda's face design on his own features and added some touches of Albert Einstein to complete the effect."
